  "definition": "Spacecraft detumbling reduces body angular rates after launch-vehicle separation, deployment, an anomaly or loss of control. It brings the vehicle into the rate and sensor-acquisition envelope needed for sun acquisition, attitude estimation and finer pointing modes. Rate damping alone does not determine absolute attitude or prove that the next control mode is available.",
